# Git branches

When creating a branch for tracked work (features, fixes, chores tied to an issue), use:

```text
feature/issue-<number>-<short-kebab-description>
```

Examples:

- `feature/issue-2-git-lfs-labview-hygiene`
- `feature/issue-14-parse-vi-cache`

Rules:

- **`<number>`** — GitHub issue number (required when an issue exists).
- **`<short-kebab-description>`** — a few words, lowercase, hyphens; matches the issue title intent.
- For **bugfixes** tied to an issue, prefer `fix/issue-<num>-<description>`.

Do not use vague names like `feature/update` or `wip` when an issue number applies.

If there is **no** GitHub issue yet, either open one first or use a temporary branch name and rename after creating the issue.
